# CLAUDE.local.md — example

> Copy this file to `CLAUDE.local.md` (drop the `.example`). That copy is git-ignored — it
> never leaves your machine. Keep secrets *by reference* here; never paste secret values.
> Actual keys belong in environment variables.

## API keys — optional; set as environment variables (do NOT paste values here)
Only needed if you switch on the optional research tools (`.mcp.json`). Set each via Windows
Settings → System → Environment Variables (then restart the Claude app so it can see them), or
your shell profile on Mac/Linux. Tick when done:

- [ ] `COMPANIES_HOUSE_API_KEY` — free, register at developer.company-information.service.gov.uk
- [ ] `EXA_API_KEY` — exa.ai (free tier exists)
- [ ] `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY` — firecrawl.dev
- [ ] `GITHUB_PAT` — optional; only if you enable the GitHub MCP server (github.com → Settings → Developer settings → personal access token, scope: repo)

## My situation
Employment status, hours a week for this venture, cash available to invest, risk tolerance,
other commitments. The brain uses this to calibrate recommendations — five hours a week and
£500 is a different venture from twenty hours and £5k.

## Machine notes
- Python (optional): runs the four optional helper hooks in `.claude/hooks/` if `start` switched them on.
- Node (optional): runs the research tools in `.mcp.json`.
- `uv` is only needed for the optional `basic-memory` MCP server.
- This folder lives at: {{ABSOLUTE_PATH}}

## Personal scratch
Anything you want the brain to see but never commit — half-formed ideas, reminders, draft
numbers, "I'm wobbling on whether to continue". Clear it whenever.

## Do not surface unprompted
Anything you would rather the brain not raise unless you raise it first.
